  "body": "Based on `upstream/main` `3e47b898b`.\n\n## What changed\n- Updated `selection::drive_chains` in `crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs` and `operation::material_region::drive_chains_of` in `crates/app/src/operation/material_region.rs` to transform picked edges through `setup_align::pose_in`.\n- Updated `fixture::rotary_axis_of` in `crates/app/src/fixture.rs` to read facets through `setup_align::facets_in`.\n- Added `Contour5D`, `Parallel5D`, `Swarf`, `AdvancedSwarf`, `RotaryContour`, `RotaryParallel`, `RotaryOffset`, `MultiAxisRough`, `Flow5D`, and `MultiAxisContour` to `setup_align::verified_kind` in `crates/app/src/setup_align.rs`.\n- Updated `setup_align::generation_problem` and module documentation to list all ten verified kinds.\n- Added nine pinning tests in `crates/app/tests/setup_align_multiaxis.rs` and recorded decisions in `docs/decisions/2286-aligned-setup-multiaxis.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- `setup_align::verified_kind` refused all ten 5-axis and rotary operations in `generation_problem`.\n- Two remaining world readers bypassed setup alignment: `selection::drive_chains` called `model::transform_of` for `MultiAxisContour` edges, and `fixture::rotary_axis_of` called `model::world_facets` to fit a rotary axis.\n\n## Tests\n- On unchanged `upstream/main`, `setup_align_multiaxis` failed (`0 passed; 7 failed`) at `setup_align::generation_problem`.\n- All 9 tests in `crates/app/tests/setup_align_multiaxis.rs` pass (`38.41s`), matching `[90, 0, 90]` and oblique `[35, 25, 40]` aligned setups against baked parts across toolpaths (`from`, `to`, `axis`), posted NC programs, fitted rotary axes, fixed workholding clearance (`RotaryContour`), and divergence or refusal on the unaligned part:\n  - `turned_contour5d_cuts_and_posts_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_parallel5d_cuts_and_posts_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_flow5d_cuts_and_posts_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_swarf_and_advanced_swarf_cut_and_post_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_multiaxis_rough_cuts_and_posts_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_rotary_contour_cuts_posts_and_fits_axis_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_rotary_parallel_cuts_posts_and_fits_axis_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_rotary_offset_cuts_posts_and_fits_axis_like_the_baked_part`\n  - `turned_multiaxis_contour_routes_drive_chains_through_setup_frame`\n- Mutation checks verified each code guard before the final doc-comment update:\n  - Reverting `selection::drive_chains` to `model::transform_of` failed `turned_multiaxis_contour_routes_drive_chains_through_setup_frame` (`picked chain 1 stands at z -5.000, outside the window [1.500, 3.000]`); restoring `pose_in` passed (`2.73s`).\n  - Reverting `fixture::rotary_axis_of` to `model::world_facets` failed `turned_rotary_parallel_cuts_posts_and_fits_axis_like_the_baked_part` (`RotaryParallel: axis [0.0, 0.0, 1.0]`); restoring `facets_in` passed (`9.40s`).\n  - Removing the ten variants from `setup_align::verified_kind` failed all 9 `setup_align_multiaxis` tests (`0 passed; 9 failed`); restoring them passed all 9 (`197.41s`).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed after the final edit (`wall 11.2 min, 51 step(s), 0 failed`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed after the final edit with zero warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n- I did not run a real CNC machine or physical rotary controller.\n- 5-axis tests posted on a synthetic A+B machine without rotary speed limits, and `RotaryContour` and `RotaryOffset` mounted `assets/machines/tilthead.mch` at post time after unmounted generation.\n- Full `gate batch` and `gate release` suites outside the 51-step quick gate were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n`crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs` is also changed by open PR #2256 (`needs-rework`, `conflicts`). PR #2256 modifies the `resolve_chain` call inside `drive_chains`, while this PR changes `drive_chains`'s `setup` parameter and the `setup_align::pose_in` lookup; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Support all ten 5-axis and rotary operations in aligned setups, including turned drive chains and fitted rotary axes.\nEffort: max\nFixes #2286\n",
